    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Castricius</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tius</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman gentile name</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 80, § 185</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. Fl. 23, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Att. 12, 28, 3 al.</span></i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Castriciānus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tiānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>pertaining to a
			Castricius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 12, 28, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fl. 23, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mendum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 2, 7, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
